{"event_type":"review","id":"71e62f26e4dcd9ddac84e981705763b7cb79cf45dadeb6ccee4195c8aa13ff7d","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T10:29:37Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6ffd5598845385dce5cf8153db0738fb44d68ac83a94d7b660e0c85f180080f9","sha256":"6ffd5598845385dce5cf8153db0738fb44d68ac83a94d7b660e0c85f180080f9"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3c1999f18bcace6f08f9548582db2eb74cfdab8515390b4f32727deea7bf655b","sha256":"3c1999f18bcace6f08f9548582db2eb74cfdab8515390b4f32727deea7bf655b"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e367ca91dc6274a5a06be5ce49040252cb15a860a802794018f75a59e74285ca","sha256":"e367ca91dc6274a5a06be5ce49040252cb15a860a802794018f75a59e74285ca"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/19280cf1bc4c8411d4afce0101b057c79fad1508f7baf0d1bb7c16f874867dab","sha256":"19280cf1bc4c8411d4afce0101b057c79fad1508f7baf0d1bb7c16f874867dab"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1178c61800d562a8194e92b914a62565432156b14f87eab5aa7062d5c7d33d03","sha256":"1178c61800d562a8194e92b914a62565432156b14f87eab5aa7062d5c7d33d03"}],"attempt_id":"a30f8af3720cbb2e629d5eb47a02d249e177d006476c88d2e0f929791c7934ef:0:1","base":"de135be6bf47236d2eda42d16031b99f5e249429","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"89fc90e2a88b231e75d55287dc4f65d3a095aa63","body":"**Bind `baseSha` to `RATCHET_MEASURED_SHA`. The measured-commit check is incomplete.**\n\nThe workflow header says the measured SHA must equal the trust SHA, \"so stale measurements cannot propose a baseline for newer code\". That check runs only at the start of the job (`ratchet-propose.yml:90`). This script then fetches a fresh `origin/main` at Line 342. If `main` advances in between, `baseSha` is a newer commit than the one measured.\n\nIn that case the script compares the old reading against the newer tip's baselines. It also cuts the proposal branch from the newer code. The PR body still says \"Measured commit: X\".\n\nThe PR checks would likely reject a too-tight proposal. The invariant is still not enforced here. Fail closed, or no-op, when the SHAs differ.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n if (/^[0-9a-f]{40,64}$/.test(baseSha ?? '') === false) {\n   fail(`origin/${BASE} did not resolve to a commit`);\n }\n+if (measuredSha !== undefined && baseSha !== measuredSha) {\n+  console.error(\n+    `ratchet-propose: ${BASE} moved from measured ${measuredSha} to ${baseSha}; ` +\n+      'stale measurement, nothing proposed',\n+  );\n+  process.exit(0);\n+}\n```\n</details>","id":"0298eae90c73550b237fdd6547f6dfbcd9c52b5c95f748abe41cbb296881a32c","intervals":[],"path":"scripts/ratchet-propose.mjs","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Bind `baseSha` to `RATCHETMEASUREDSHA`. The measured-commit check is incomplete."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"a2d7eb56f92df67d87389f25b4e85b719915779c","body":"**Use `--tree` in the release runbook.**\n\n`docs/0.2-release-runbook.md:83` runs `denylist-scan` without a flag from an unpacked package. No-argument mode selects `outgoingScan`, which requires Git history. This can fail because the unpacked package has no `.git` directory.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-(cd \"$unpack_dir/package\" && DENYLIST_SCAN_NO_DIST_ALLOWLIST=1 ./scripts/denylist-scan)\n+(cd \"$unpack_dir/package\" && DENYLIST_SCAN_NO_DIST_ALLOWLIST=1 ./scripts/denylist-scan --tree)\n```\n\n</details>","id":"6b29bcad330f1528e7b929151bae92fabf3598f26d3f4c2f8779aa46a47ba03d","intervals":[],"path":"scripts/denylist-scan","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Use `--tree` in the release runbook."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"a2d7eb56f92df67d87389f25b4e85b719915779c","body":"**Do not reuse the working-tree allowlist for committed content.**\n\n`outgoingScan` passes every committed blob of each outgoing commit to `treeConfigToml(rules)`. That config allowlists `(^|/)dist/`, `(^|/)node_modules/`, and `(^|/)\\.gjc/`. A committed file under one of these paths that contains a denylist string is dropped before it is reported, so the publish gate can pass it. The `dist/`, `node_modules/`, and `.gjc/` exemptions cover working-tree build output, not committed content.\n\nUse a config for outgoing scans that allowlists only the copied `patterns.yml` and keeps `[extend] useDefault = true`:\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔒️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        const { res, findings } = runScan(tmp, `${commit}-${label}`, treeConfigToml(rules), '.', { cwd });\n+        const { res, findings } = runScan(tmp, `${commit}-${label}`, outgoingConfigToml(rules), '.', { cwd });\n```\n\nAdd this helper next to `treeConfigToml`:\n\n```js\nfunction outgoingConfigToml(rules) {\n  // Tracked blobs only: no dist/, node_modules/, .gjc/ exemptions. The\n  // patterns.yml copy stays allowlisted, as in the tree config.\n  let out = '# Generated by scripts/denylist-scan from policy/denylist/patterns.yml -- do not edit.\\n\\n';\n  out += '[[allowlists]]\\n' + pathEntries([PATTERNS_ALLOW_RE]) + '\\n\\n';\n  out += '[extend]\\nuseDefault = true\\n\\n';\n  out += rulesToml(rules);\n  return out;\n}\n```\n\n</details>","id":"8b8e4b80a81aab5364e37fc7b5d4195714729b40a380d937c6818d8cf86ac956","intervals":[],"path":"scripts/denylist-scan","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Do not reuse the working-tree allowlist for committed content."}],"head":"1f19d297e8a718d5e1185ba1403a3900c2a30ece","head_tree":"caf2bd1c0f6a76b490442f34307539ee3268e814","input_scope":[{"blob":"40d5ec899f3adf76657bd3b61f12c5110f9165b4","intervals":[[1,156]],"path":".github/workflows/ratchet-propose.yml"},{"blob":"03fe2ce727dce5082d7aeba7d1e5db6d70ccffeb","intervals":[[1,135]],"path":".github/workflows/ratchet.yml"},{"blob":"a4167559c828ba803b83931b982c252e01d90a82","intervals":[[3,3],[5,8],[10,10],[22,23],[26,29],[31,42],[47,50],[53,55],[66,74]],"path":"package.json"},{"blob":"aaec220837e5d40edcf6cdbca8eb1978d714c9c7","intervals":[[4,4],[6,6],[10,11],[14,18],[32,32],[34,35],[42,47],[49,49],[51,54],[56,57],[59,64],[79,80],[98,108],[170,171]],"path":"policy/DOCTRINE.md"},{"blob":"538b8c3b7289de86098d3bb189a5d09fdb95e5ce","intervals":[[1,1],[3,4],[8,10],[22,62],[66,68],[72,77],[81,84]],"path":"policy/templates/README.md"},{"blob":"a2d7eb56f92df67d87389f25b4e85b719915779c","intervals":[[7,7],[18,24],[48,50],[75,75],[82,95],[159,163],[171,175],[240,300],[348,348],[588,637],[809,810],[948,955],[958,960],[1077,1094],[1097,1097],[1100,1101],[1106,1106],[1111,1111],[1115,1115],[1118,1130],[1132,1132],[1136,1136],[1139,1140],[1146,1151],[1153,1153],[1155,1155],[1158,1159],[1172,1178],[1184,1250],[1262,1263],[1284,1287],[1309,1491],[1505,1508],[1513,1516],[1563,1566],[1570,1573],[1579,1583]],"path":"scripts/denylist-scan"},{"blob":"6b9f2eefaee5163c8a3e4089c53f399c13f03956","intervals":[[1,568]],"path":"scripts/ratchet-lib.mjs"},{"blob":"89fc90e2a88b231e75d55287dc4f65d3a095aa63","intervals":[[1,671]],"path":"scripts/ratchet-propose.mjs"}],"job_id":"a30f8af3720cbb2e629d5eb47a02d249e177d006476c88d2e0f929791c7934ef:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"5596c475bee198de2f3d8820aa654e8cd3c5ba47","kind":"blob","mode":"100755","path":"scripts/denylist-scan"},"merge":"db1be774a51130637c31c5932e0099b3c8602878","method":"pre-merge","pre":"fd67d5a2104276e928378582a5bdb94a05cfd99c","source_path":"scripts/denylist-scan"},"blob":"a2d7eb56f92df67d87389f25b4e85b719915779c","disposition":"included","mode":"100755","path":"scripts/denylist-scan","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"entry":null,"merge":"db1be774a51130637c31c5932e0099b3c8602878","method":"pre-merge","pre":"fd67d5a2104276e928378582a5bdb94a05cfd99c","source_path":".